            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "§5. Linear Functionals"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.844,
            0.056,
            0.869,
            0.07
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "75"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.099,
            0.871,
            0.211
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "it suffices, since "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "C _ { b } ( B )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is complete (1.6), to show that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\rho ( \\mathcal { X } ^ { * } )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is closed. Let "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\left\\{ f _ { n } \\right\\} \\subseteq { \\mathcal { X } } ^ { * }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and suppose "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "g   \\in   \\bar { C } _ { b } ( B )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " such that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\| \\rho ( f _ { n } ) - g \\| \\to 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " as "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n   \\rightarrow   \\infty"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Let "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x { \\in } { \\mathcal { X } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . If "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\alpha , \\beta \\in \\mathbb { F } , \\alpha , \\beta \\neq 0 ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " such that αx, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\beta x { \\in } B ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " then "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\alpha ^ { - 1 } g ( \\alpha x ) ="
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " lim "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\alpha^{-1} f_n(\\alpha x) ="
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " lim "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\beta ^ { - 1 } f _ { n } ( \\beta x ) = \\beta ^ { - 1 } g ( \\beta x )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Define "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "f \\colon { \\mathcal { X } }   \\to   \\mathbb { F }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " by letting "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "f(x) = \\alpha^{-1} g(\\alpha x)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for any "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\alpha \\neq 0"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " such that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\alpha x { \\in } B ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " It is left as an exercise for the reader to show that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "f \\in \\mathcal { X } ^ { * }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\rho ( f )   =   g"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " ■"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.227,
            0.629,
            0.245
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Compare the preceding result with Exercise 2.1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.246,
            0.871,
            0.303
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "It should be emphasized that it is not assumed in the preceding proposition that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathcal { X }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is complete. In fact, if "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathcal { X }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is a normed space and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\hat { \\mathcal { X } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is its completion (Exercise 1.16), then "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathcal { X } ^ { * }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\hat { \\mathcal { X } } ^ { * }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are isometrically isomorphic (Exercise 2.2)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.319,
            0.874,
            0.358
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5.5. Theorem. Let "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( X , \\Omega , \\mu )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " be a measure space and let "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 < p < \\infty"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . If "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 / p + 1 / q = 1"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "g   \\in   L ^ { q } ( X , \\Omega , \\mu ) ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " define "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "F _ { g } \\colon L ^ { p } ( \\mu ) \\to \\mathbb { F } \\; b y"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.416,
            0.364,
            0.579,
            0.407
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_89_equation_6.jpg",
          "content": "F _ { g } ( f ) = \\int f g   d \\mu ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.413,
            0.87,
            0.452
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Then "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "F _ { g } \\in L ^ { p } ( \\mu ) ^ { * }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and the map "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "g   \\mapsto   F _ { g }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " defines an isometric isomorphism of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "L ^ { \\pmb { q } } ( \\mu )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " onto "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "L ^ { p } ( \\mu ) ^ { * }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.469,
            0.87,
            0.526
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since this theorem is often proved in courses in measure and integration the proof of this result, as well as the next two, is contained in the Appendix. See Appendix B for the proofs of (5.5) and (5.6)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.542,
            0.87,
            0.58
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5.6. Theorem. "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "I f ( X , \\Omega , \\mu )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is a σ-finite measure space and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "g { \\in } L ^ { \\infty } ( X , \\Omega , \\mu )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , define "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "F _ { g } : L ^ { 1 } ( \\mu ) \\to \\mathbb { F } b y"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.416,
            0.586,
            0.578,
            0.629
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_89_equation_10.jpg",
          "content": "F _ { g } ( f ) = \\int f g   d \\mu ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.635,
            0.869,
            0.673
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Then "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "F _ { g }   \\in   L ^ { 1 } ( \\mu ) ^ { * }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and the map "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "g   \\mapsto   F _ { g }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " defines an isometric isomorphism of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "L ^ { \\infty } ( \\mu )"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " onto "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "L ^ { 1 ^ { \\circ } } ( \\mu ) ^ { * }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.69,
            0.87,
            0.764
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Note that when "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "p = 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " in Theorem 5.5, there is a little difference between (5.5) and (I.3.5) owing to the absence of a complex conjugate in (5.5). Also, note that (5.6) is false if the measure space is not assumed to be σ-finite (Exercise 3)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.763,
            0.871,
            0.82
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If X is a locally compact space, M(X) denotes the space of all F-valued regular Borel measures on X with the total variation norm. See Appendix C for the definitions as well as the proof of the next theorem."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.845,
            0.871,
            0.883
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5.7. Riesz Representation Theorem. If X is a locally compact space and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mu { \\in } M ( X ) ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , define "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "F _ { \\mu } \\colon C _ { 0 } ( X ) \\to \\mathbb { F } \\; b y"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.423,
            0.889,
            0.575,
            0.932
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_89_equation_15.jpg",
          "content": "F _ { \\mu } ( f ) = \\int f d \\mu ."
        }
      ]
    }
